<BaseLayout title="About PARADOX" description="How PARADOX evaluates public GitHub evidence, what its scores mean, and what they do not mean." canonical="https://paradox.engineer/about/">
  <main class="legal">
    <p class="label">ABOUT / METHODOLOGY</p>
    <h1>Useful evidence, clearly labeled.</h1>
    <article>
      <p>PARADOX helps developers and AI builders discover public AI agents, skills and GitHub projects, then inspect observable repository evidence before they depend on them.</p>
      <h2>How analysis works</h2>
      <p>The verifier reads public GitHub metadata and a limited set of files, including README files, manifests, Docker files and workflows. It runs deterministic static analysis. Repository contents are treated as untrusted data; instructions inside repository text are never followed.</p>
      <h2>What the evidence status means</h2>
      <p><strong>Evidence-supported</strong> means the repository was public and analyzable at the time of the scan, the available evidence met PARADOX's current documentation/health criteria, and the current static rules did not identify enough high-risk indicators to place it in a higher-risk state.</p>
      <p><strong>Needs review</strong> means the evidence is mixed or insufficient for the stronger status. <strong>Stale evidence</strong> means repository activity or freshness signals are old. <strong>High-risk signals</strong> means the current static rules found indicators that deserve investigation.</p>
      <h2>What these labels do not mean</h2>
      <p>None of these labels certify software. They are not security certifications, penetration-test results, formal code reviews, or guarantees that a project is safe to install or run. A repository can contain malicious, vulnerable or obfuscated behavior that the current rules do not detect.</p>
      <h2>Scores and unknowns</h2>
      <p>PARADOX scores summarize observable signals such as repository health, freshness, documentation, activity and static risk indicators. A missing detector match is treated as <strong>unknown</strong>, not proof that a model, tool, vulnerability or behavior is absent.</p>
      <h2>Data freshness</h2>
      <p>Repository evidence can change immediately after a scan. Stars, forks, issues, commits, releases, files and permissions can all change independently of PARADOX. Always open the source repository and review its current state before making a high-impact decision.</p>
      <h2>Source methodology</h2>
      <p>Discovery uses the curated catalog plus GitHub Search. Trending uses recent GitHub activity and explicit catalog signals. PARADOX does not claim search volume, endorsements or safety unless it has corresponding evidence.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
